Based on the analysis of the provided data and logs, it seems that the current implementation lacks a mechanism for ensuring the generated solutions are accurate and robust. One approach to improving this is by incorporating the `Test` operator to validate the generated code against a set of predefined test cases before returning the solution. This would help in catching any logical errors or edge cases that the initial generation might miss.

To achieve this, we will modify the graph to include a step where the generated code is tested and validated before finalizing the solution.

